# International > Time Format (dialog 16): 24 hour with the suffix "h", separator ".", leading zero,
# OK, then OK in International (tab from Change... to OK) - WIN.INI [intl] is written. Same keys as
# arch311-ref/scn/intl-time.scn after opening. Run as intl.w16 (ARCH311_REF_INI=1,
# ARCH311_CLOCK="2026-10-08 09:30:24", applet International). The reference's time sample read :42
# after the Time Format OK, 18 s after the dialog opened: the long pause puts the port's OK in :42.
# regress: ARCH311_REF_INI=1 ARCH311_CLOCK="2026-10-08 09:30:24" sh tools/run-cp-test.sh "$TEST" "$OUT" International
# compare: intl-time/02.png 01-open.png active ignore 320 240 332 260
# compare: intl-time/03.png 02-time.png active ignore 320 240 332 260
# compare: intl-time/04.png 03-24hour.png active ignore 320 240 332 260
# compare: intl-time/05.png 04-changed.png active ignore 320 240 332 260
# compare: intl-time/06.png 05-sample.png active ignore 320 240 332 260
# ini: WIN.INI intl iTime=1
# ini: WIN.INI intl iTLZero=1
# ini: WIN.INI intl s1159=h
# ini: WIN.INI intl s2359=h
# ini: WIN.INI intl sTime=.
sleep 900
shot shots/01-open.png
key tab
key tab
key tab
key tab
key tab
key tab
key tab
key enter
sleep 600
shot shots/02-time.png
key down
sleep 300
shot shots/03-24hour.png
key tab
type h
key tab
type .
key tab
key right
sleep 300
shot shots/04-changed.png
sleep 16000
key enter
sleep 500
shot shots/05-sample.png
key tab
key tab
key enter
sleep 400
quit
